  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of $x^8$ in the expansion of\n$$P(x)=(x+1)(x+2)\\cdots(x+10).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1320$.\n\nChoose the constant terms from two factors and $x$ from the other eight; sum the products of the chosen constants.",
      "worked": "Each $x^8$ term comes from choosing constants from two factors and $x$ from the remaining eight. Its coefficient is therefore $\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le10}ij$.\n\nUsing the expansion of a square,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(1+2+\\cdots+10)^2&=1^2+2^2+\\cdots+10^2+2\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le10}ij,\\\\\n\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le10}ij&=\\frac{55^2-385}{2},\\\\\n\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le10}ij&=1320.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe coefficient of $x^8$ is $1320$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
